<MainLayout title="October 20 West Covina Agenda: Funding, Parks & Public Safety | StayJustIn" description="Source-backed reporting on Fire Station 1, street sweeping, Altamira, Verdugo dispatch, police technology, playgrounds, traffic signals, and storm preparation." canonical="https://www.stayjustin.com/city-hall/october-20-2026-agenda-report/">
  <section class="section"><div class="container"><article class="briefing">
    <p class="page-kicker">City Hall / October 20 records</p>
    <h1>What West Covina’s latest records say about funding, services, and unfinished projects</h1>
    <ArticleMetadata category="Agenda review" published="October 23, 2026" />
    <p>The October 20 packet documents a Fire Station 1 design hold, proposed spending on hillside evaluation and playground equipment, and a long-term fire-dispatch agreement. It also reports completed traffic-signal work and planning for Galster fire mitigation.</p>
    <p><strong>What is verified:</strong> the contents of the staff reports and project presentation, plus the City’s current street-sweeping notice. <strong>What is not verified here:</strong> October 20 vote results, executed agreements, or subsequent payments. A recommendation in an agenda is not proof of approval.</p>
    <h2>Three details that change the reading</h2>
    <ul>
      <li>The fire-dispatch fiscal paragraph contains an <strong>account number</strong>, not a $110,502.32 spending cap. Its draft also permits exceptions to the ordinary 5% annual rate-increase limit.</li>
      <li>The signage presentation says <strong>Phase I</strong> is complete and lists <strong>Phase II</strong> as upcoming. It does not say the entire street-sweeping transition is finished.</li>
      <li>The $223,980.25 traffic-signal budget difference is measured against the construction budget <strong>including contingency</strong>. Actual construction exceeded the original contract amount.</li>
    </ul>
    <p>The common thread is practical: what was budgeted, what has actually happened, what remains unfunded, and what record would answer the next question.</p>
    <p><a href={agendaUrl}>Official agenda</a> · <a href={sourcePdf}>Selected source records (PDF, about 5 MB)</a> · <a href="/accountability/budget-spending/">Budget tracker</a></p>
  </article></div></section>
  <OctoberCoverage />
</MainLayout>
